{"cases":[{"target_alias":"SRC_001","attack":true,"case":"The target asserts that no autonomous reclamation protocol is safe, but it overlooks an autonomous preserve-then-reclaim strategy: the protocol can unconditionally durably record the entire workspace contents (or a binding cryptographic commitment to them) before reclamation. Because any completed evidence would be preserved in that durable record, such a protocol would never silently displace evidence and meets the problem's guarantee without an external witness. By missing this possibility, the target incorrectly mandates an external witness and misidentifies what must be durably recorded—substituting a signed attestation of evidence absence for the actual workspace state that a safe autonomous protocol would preserve."}]}